# Anchor Browser Docs

> ## Agent Instructions
> Anchor Browser is cloud browser infrastructure for AI agents and automation: browser sessions you control over CDP or REST, natural-language web tasks, versioned automation tasks, managed authentication into third-party web apps (identities with MFA), persistent volumes and profiles, recordings, live view, batch sessions, webhooks, and network options including residential proxies, extra stealth, and captcha solving for sites that block standard browsers. AI agents should start at https://docs.anchorbrowser.io/for-agents, then get an API key with Agent Access at https://docs.anchorbrowser.io/quickstart/agent-access — no dashboard account required. Read those two pages before authentication or API calls.

- [Documentation](https://docs.anchorbrowser.io/introduction.md): Cloud browsers for AI agents and automation: sessions over CDP or REST, natural-language web tasks, managed authentication, volumes, recordings, batch sessions, and stealth browsing. Get a key at https://docs.anchorbrowser.io/quickstart/agent-access.
- [Agent Access](https://docs.anchorbrowser.io/quickstart/agent-access.md): Self-serve API key for agents. Solve a short puzzle — no dashboard account required.
- [SDK Quick Start](https://docs.anchorbrowser.io/quickstart/use-via-sdk.md)
- [Code Quick Start](https://docs.anchorbrowser.io/quickstart/use-via-code.md)
- [API Quick Start](https://docs.anchorbrowser.io/quickstart/use-via-api.md)
- [Task Examples](https://docs.anchorbrowser.io/examples/task-examples.md): Browse ready-made task examples in the Anchor library.
